React Router v8 framework mode (v7.18 same). Status comes from what is thrown, before streaming: an unmatched URL or `throw data(null, { status: 404 | 410 | 503 })` gives that status, any other thrown Error gives 500, and the root ErrorBoundary only renders it. Never `catch` a dependency error in a loader and return data or throw a 404 (RTE-007), and keep `status: responseStatusCode` in entry.server.tsx. `Layout` wraps the ErrorBoundary, so the chrome is shared; keep it free of loader data.
